course: dictionary
lesson: 12250
title: Long words, clear parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are easier than they look. Constitutionally has three parts: constitution, -al and -ly. A constitution is a country's main set of laws and rules. The endings turn it into an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done.
explain: «The new rule was checked, and it was constitutionally allowed.» The rule was checked against the country's main laws, and it passed. So constitutionally means in a way that follows the constitution. Swap in "in a way that follows the constitution" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe a person's nature. «She is constitutionally unable to keep a secret.» Here it means it is part of who she is, from her natural character, not from any law. The words around it, unable and keep a secret, are the clues.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to choose. Ask: is the sentence about laws, rules or a country? Then the law meaning fits. Is it about a person and what they can or cannot do? Then the character meaning fits.
fact: A constitution is a country's main set of laws and rules.
fact: «Constitutionally» means in a way that follows or is allowed by a constitution.
fact: «Constitutionally» can also mean coming from someone's natural body or character, as in «constitutionally unable to sit still».
fact: Breaking a long word into parts, like constitution plus -al plus -ly, helps you work out what it means.
fact: In the USA, the Supreme Court decides whether a law is constitutional.
exercise: «The judges said the new law was not constitutionally allowed.» What does constitutionally mean here? | Slowly and carefully | In a way that comes from a person's natural character | *In a way that follows the country's main laws | Very loudly
exercise: «Sam is constitutionally unable to sit still for long.» What does this suggest about Sam? | He is very old | A new law has been passed about him | *It is part of his natural character | He is a judge
exercise: Which word is the base of constitutionally? | consider | constant | *constitution | constable
test: «The club was constitutionally set up to help children.» What does this sentence mean? | The club was set up by accident | The club was set up at the seaside | *The club was set up in a way that follows the country's rules | The club was set up to help only adults
test: «My little brother is constitutionally a night owl.» What does constitutionally mean here? | He is a famous judge | *Because of his natural character, he likes staying up late | He lost his way in the night | Because a law says he must stay up late
exam: What are the two meanings of constitutionally? | Very old, and very wet | Only just, and very quiet | Very quickly, and very loudly | *In a way that follows a country's constitution, and in a way that comes from someone's natural character
